From 7d2b2153e8907a3615e01df9d45e405bd4ca35e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:21:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 261/269] gallium/pvr: compute fallback draw integrated into
 pipe_context - draw_vbo renders on the GPU

Adds the compute fallback as a first-class part of the driver:
- new pvr_compute.c/h: builds the compute fallback state lazily per context from the embedded triangle
  SPIR-V (compiled by pco through spirv_to_nir), generates the PDS kernel/fence/descriptor programs with
  libpowervr_pds, allocates all dispatch buffers from the real heaps through pvr_vm_heap_alloc (general
  pages for descriptor set/literals, CDM control stream, context state, border table; a PDS page for the
  programs; a USC page for the shader), builds the 22-dword CDM control stream and 44-byte compute fw
  stream from the generated programs, creates a compute context with minimal static state and submits
  through pvr_job_submit_compute_sync();
- pvr_context.c's draw_vbo now executes the draw: when a colour buffer is bound it patches the descriptor
  set with that render target and submits the compute job (draws_executed tracks it), instead of warning
  that nothing will be drawn; the compute state is torn down with the context;
- the probe gains PVR_PROBE_COMPUTE_DRAW=1, which drives the whole path through the pipe_context API:
  create context, create a 512x512 RGBA8 render target, set_framebuffer_state, draw_vbo(3 vertices), map
  and read back -> inside=73728 pixels, centre=0xFF0000FF, corner=0xFFFF0000, PASS with 1 draw executed.
Verified on hardware: with the env var the probe prints draw PASS and --- ALL PASS; without it and on the
drm-shim it still prints --- ALL PASS. (Limitation for now: the compute fallback renders to 512x512 RGBA8
targets only; everything larger falls back to the warning path. Fixed-function 3D/TA remains unusable.)
